<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria Co-op bank posts 6.5 mln lev loss in 1996.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria Co-op bank posts 6.5 mln lev loss in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Central Co-operative Bank (CCB) posted a 6.5 million lev loss for 1996, which added to losses from previous years, bringing the total to 649.6 million levs, figures published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for 1995 were unavailable.</p>
<p>Figures from the bank's profit and loss account and balance sheet follow in million levs unless stated otherwise:</p>
<p>								 1996</p>
<p> Total revenue					36,976.992</p>
<p> Net interest income				  -662.194</p>
<p> Net income on government securities	     -24.958</p>
<p> Net income on commissions and</p>
<p> foreign currency translation gains	    2,089.200</p>
<p> Business and administration costs		 948.953</p>
<p> Provisions						668.096</p>
<p> Taxes							 6.483</p>
<p> Loss							  6.483</p>
<p> Cumulative loss					 649.550</p>
<p> Total assets					 17,821.208</p>
<p> Cash						    2,522.834</p>
<p> Treasury securities portfolio		     939.162</p>
<p> Extended interbank deposits		     2,368.302</p>
<p> Attracted interbank deposits		    3,151.979</p>
<p> Lending to non-financial clients		8,169.944</p>
<p>Attracted deposits from non-financial</p>
<p> clients						12,073.743</p>
<p> Stakes in other companies			 1,441.319</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity				2,000.000</p>
<p> Capital, including provisions and reserves  2,676.896</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
